Root cause:
The bug was caused by the assumption that northbound plugins would automatically apply the mask to IPv4 prefixes. This led to situations where the prefixes were not properly masked before being processed, resulting in incorrect behavior. Additionally, there was a bug in the "distance" command that was introduced in a previous commit, which was also addressed in this patch. Furthermore, unnecessary checks in the route map deletion function were removed to ensure the route map's pointer was reset for safety, preventing potential issues related to dangling pointers.
